new file mode 100644
index 0000000..82f46e4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/BANGUMI.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Built-in Bangumi metadata
+
+Bangumi (bgm.tv) is built into this fork as a native anime metadata source, beside AniList, MyAnimeList and Simkl. Select **Bangumi** in the Home source menu or in Settings → Modules. No module URL, script, or Bangumi account is needed; metadata and artwork are read from the public `api.bgm.tv/v0` API.
+
+`BangumiService` is plain Swift: it does not run JavaScript and ships no script resources. Titles carry `ProviderType.bangumi` and their Bangumi subject id (`bangumi-<id>`).
+
+Home shows Bangumi's score ranking and premiere-date catalogs. Search finds anime by keyword, subject link or `bgm:<id>`. Title pages show titles, cover art, synopsis, rating, rank, tags, studios, directors and main episodes. To watch, use the page's playback-source picker, which searches your installed playback modules for the title and its aliases.
+
+## Why Bangumi is not in the AniList/MyAnimeList chain
+
+Like Simkl, Bangumi is a discovery source kept outside `ProviderManager`. Bangumi subject ids are not AniList or MyAnimeList ids, and the AniList title page keys tracking, Continue Watching and library sync on AniList ids. Bangumi titles therefore open their own page and are never sent to a tracker. Profile, notifications and library keep using the signed-in AniList or MyAnimeList account whichever Home source is chosen. Saving a Bangumi title stores it in My Library.
+
+## Upgrading from the imported module
+
+Earlier versions ran the `bangumi.js` module, imported or bundled, in a JavaScript context. A saved choice of that module now becomes the built-in source automatically. Imported copies are hidden, are never run, and cannot be chosen for playback or downloads. Other installed metadata modules keep working.
+
+## Source and validation
+
+The fork starts at upstream commit `398d36715b34a17ec68bfd52d792f7a2e7db06f5`. The complete patch and build workflow are maintained in [quiteQa/shirox-bangumi](https://github.com/quiteQa/shirox-bangumi/tree/main/native).
+
+The workflow checks localization and icons, builds all four app schemes, and compiles the iOS tests without a simulator. `MetadataModuleTests` covers Bangumi subject, episode and page decoding, adult and non-anime filtering, subject links, legacy-module handling and source selection across profile reloads.
+
+XCTest has not been executed and real-device behavior has not been verified. Existing libzstd module-import and AppIntents metadata warnings remain. The upstream `TSAudioTimestampsTests` expression is split into intermediate values to avoid a type-check timeout without changing its behavior.
